---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Method — unt·ded"
  description="How the UNTDED 2005 PDF was digitized and how every element can be verified: character conservation, row reconciliation, OCR re-reads, UN/EDIFACT cross-check."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Method</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-body">
      The 2005 edition exists as a 132-page scan. The digitization parses the
      page text layer by word coordinates, reassembles wrapped cells, and then
      proves the result with checks that are independent of the extraction
      code. Everything below runs in the open:
      <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href="https://github.com/untded/untded-2005">untded/untded-2005</a>.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Extraction</h2>
      <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-2 leading-relaxed text-body">
        <li>Pages 28–132 (the element table) are read with <span class="font-mono text-sm">pdftotext -bbox-layout</span>; every word carries PDF coordinates.</li>
        <li>Nine column ranges in points were calibrated from the layout (tag ≈ x68.8, UID ≈ x108.6, name ≈ x131.3, description ≈ x286.6, representation ≈ x523.1, old name ≈ x558.9, business term ≈ x612.7, bridges ≈ x705.5) — stable across all 105 table pages.</li>
        <li>Rows start where a change tag meets a four-digit tag; wrapped cells are reassembled line by line, with rules for the text layer’s mid-word breaks (slash-compounds such as “Document/message”, lone-letter tails, vocabulary-confirmed merges).</li>
        <li>The result is a YAML single source of truth, typed with lutaml-model; CSV/JSON/HTML are derived, never hand-edited.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Verification</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 space-y-4">
        <div class="rounded-md border border-line bg-mist p-4">
          <dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Character conservation — exact</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
            Joining rules can only concatenate or insert whitespace, so the
            multiset of non-space characters in the table region must equal the
            multiset in the cells. Result: <strong class="text-ink">169,020 characters, exact match</strong>
            in both stages (words → fragments → YAML).
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-md border border-line bg-mist p-4">
          <dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Row reconciliation</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
            The tag column and the UID column are independent word streams:
            <strong class="text-ink">1504 UID words = 1504 elements</strong>, per-tag counts equal.
            Regeneration is byte-identical.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-md border border-line bg-mist p-4">
          <dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Independent OCR re-read</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
            Tesseract — a different engine from whatever produced the text
            layer — re-reads random row crops from the rendered page images:
            <strong class="text-ink">names 80/80 agree</strong>, representation values 31/31 readable crops agree.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-md border border-line bg-mist p-4">
          <dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cross-source check (UN/EDIFACT D.05B)</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
            Joined against an independent electronic typesetting of the same
            element base (586 shared tags): representations agree on charset
            and length for 549/584; every image-readable difference matches
            <em>this</em> edition’s print, i.e. the diffs are the 2005
            edition’s own editorial revisions. Description differences follow
            the edition’s systematic “message”→“document” rewrite.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10" id="confidence">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Confidence labels</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
        Every element carries a provenance record: source file, PDF page, and a
        confidence grade. <strong class="text-ink">High</strong> — all cells
        single-line in the source. <strong class="text-ink">Medium</strong> —
        line-wrapped cells were re-joined (the risky narrow columns) or a
        mid-word break was repaired. <strong class="text-ink">Low</strong> —
        flagged for review (currently the four legend-external change tags).
        Current split: 472 high / 1028 medium / 4 low.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10" id="anomalies">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Anomalies we keep, not fix</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
        <li>
          The print itself orders 1481 before 1478 (p. 36) and starts page 44
          with 2141 after page 43 ended at 2159. Transcribed as printed.
        </li>
        <li>
          Element 4000’s note says “use instead — 1056”, but 1056 is not in
          this edition (the note dangles in the source itself).
        </li>
        <li>
          Four rows print change tags outside the section 4.1 legend
          (5082 “cr”, 5180 “cdr”, 5390 “cr”, 5450 “cd”). Glyph-count analysis
          of 600 dpi renders confirms the print really shows those letters.
        </li>
        <li>
          Some names print a space before a dot (“Configuration. Level
          .Identifier”) — the source’s own typography, kept verbatim.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
